<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santiago Derqui</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1809">1809</a>–<a href="/years/1867">1867</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> Derqui was an Argentine lawyer and politician who served as president of the Argentine Confederation from 1860 to 1861. His attempt to reconcile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> with the other provinces failed, and after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartolome-mitre">Bartolomé Mitre</a>'s victory at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pavon">Battle of Pavón</a> he resigned, opening the way for national reunification under Mitre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santiago-derqui.jpg" alt="Santiago Derqui" width="320" height="367" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Santiago_Derqui_1860.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
